  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 255 PM EDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\n- Showers continue until tomorrow\n\nLight to moderate rain from the persistent tropical moisture will\ncontinue through the rest of the day until tomorrow as the ribbon\nof moisture continues. Anomalous PWATS upwards of 1.75 inches are\non track to advect through the region through 00Z. So expect\nperiods of moderate showers to be possible. However, the axis of\nheavier precip will slowly move to the southeast, so not expecting\nflooding. An additional inch of precipitation is expected, with\nthe largest amounts expected along and south of the I -94\ncorridor.\n\n- Cooler weather ahead, Frost/freeze chances begin this weekend\n\nA cold front will be driving the moisture to the southeast\ntomorrow. Which will end the rainfall and usher in cooler\ntemperatures, along with some gusty northwesterly flow tomorrow. \nThis will bring cooler temperatures overall. Clear skies and \nlighter winds will set the stage for potential frost/freeze Friday\nnight, Saturday morning. Min Temps could be 5 to 10 degrees below\nnormal, especially north of I 96. Will hold off on headlines for \nnow but they will probably be needed. Temps will rebound into \nSunday, and a weak system will swing through, though any \nprecipitation should be remain through northern lower.\nTemperaturesat or below normal are ahead, with High's in the low\n60s expected through mid next week.",
